composer: grow to a second line instead of scrolling sideways

A long message scrolls out of sight in a single-line input, so you cannot re-read
what you wrote before sending it. A textarea grows with the text instead, up to a
third of the window, and drops back to one row after sending. Enter sends,
Shift+Enter breaks the line.

⚠️ Growing takes height away from the buffer, which cuts the last message off.
ScrollManager's ResizeObserver does pin it back, but only if `stickToBottom`, which
a debounced scroll handler updates 100ms late — so while you type the bottom line
keeps disappearing and settles only once you stop. Hence `keepAtBottom()`: the
composer asks before changing height and pins right after, in the same frame.

Tab completion is unchanged, except that a word now ends at any whitespace: with
newlines in play, ` ` alone left the line break inside the word.

